  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening law enforcement to protect Amur tigers in Southeast Primorye the Russian Far East</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to continue to strengthen the Spatial Monitoring And Reporting Tool (SMART) patrol approach that will monitor and mitigate the effect of illegal human activities on Amur tigers in Lazovsky State Nature Reserve (LZ) and Zov Tigra National Park (ZT). Project will support expanded SMART approach training, and the use of standard camera trapping techniques, allowing to measure the effectiveness of activities by tracking changes in tiger abundance. To minimize the risk of illegal human activities on tigers in LZ and ZT, and continue a camera trap monitoring program in ZT, LZ, and Medved Hunting lease, the project has the following objectives: (1) Strengthen and expand ZSLs support for SMART in LZ and ZT by supporting national protected area management, building capacity of park rangers and continued support for the SMART database computer specialist; (2) Continue the long-term camera trap monitoring program in ZT, LZ, and Medved Hunting lease.</narrative>
  </description>
